    <data name="AboutDescription" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Lodgeboard was started in Porto in 2017 by a hotel manager and an engineer. 85 people in Porto and Ljubljana now build it for 2,300 properties.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="AboutLede" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>We make software for the people behind the desk: owners, receptionists, housekeepers and night porters. 85 of us, in Porto and Ljubljana.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="StoryTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Started at a front desk</value>
    </data>
    <data name="StoryBody1" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Teresa Lobo ran a 40-room hotel on the Douro for nine years, with three systems that didn't talk to each other and a whiteboard that did the real work.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="StoryBody2" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>In 2017 she and Luka Horvat built that whiteboard as software: one board for arrivals, rooms and housekeeping, connected to the booking sites. Her own hotel was the first customer.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="StoryBody3" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Lodgeboard has been profitable since 2021, without outside investors, so the roadmap is written by hoteliers, not by a board.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="PrinciplesTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>How we work</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Principle1Title" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Answer like a night porter</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Principle1Body" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Hotels don't close, so neither does support. A person answers by chat or phone day and night, in a median of four minutes.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Principle2Title" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Work a shift every quarter</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Principle2Body" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Everyone at Lodgeboard, engineers included, spends a shift at a customer's front desk every three months.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Principle3Title" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Never hold your data hostage</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Principle3Body" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Bookings, guests and invoices can be exported at any time, in open formats, and moving away costs nothing.</value>
    </data>
